    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32800" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppīlo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obp-</span></b> ), āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		obpilo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to stop up</i>, <i>shut up</i> (rare
			but class; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syn.: obturo, obstruo, claudo): metretam novam
					amurcā colluito, oppilato,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 100</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, 31, 135</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 725</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scalis tabernae oppilatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clausae portae et oppilatae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2</span></i>
			 Esdr. 7, 3.</div>
